Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||01-30-2001||08:17 PM||||Hi, I'm going to start planning the Central IL Fiero Show for summer of 2001 and need a little input.  First off let me set this up, last year we had about 40 cars show up throughout the day (if everyone did sign in) even though there was rain.  It was held on Saturday, August 26th in El Paso Illinois.  I am thinking of having it a few weeks earlier this year, but don't want to interfere with any club get-togethers and really want to get more NIFE members this year.  I had several show up last year, but didn't get info to them quick enough to make their newsletter.  What date works out best during August.  It'll be a Saturday again, probably from 11AM -4 or 5pm.  I hope to have Archie, Rodney, and Bob Steiger, as well as the DL-10 predator show up again.  Maybe we could get a bigger crowd if I find a better date and post info quicker this year   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'm thinking of having prizes, awards and more this time.  If any vendors want to donate a few prizes for an attendance drawing, contact me here.  Thanks to anyone who can give any feedback, if you have ANY experiece with shows I'd like to hear from you.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Michael Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> <p>[This message has been edited by MikeSchaefer (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Oreif||01-30-2001||09:20 PM||||August 4th and 11th are open for me.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MikeSchaefer||01-30-2001||09:51 PM||||The 4th is the ideal date for me, as long as this doesn't affect any other shows in the area.  Do you know of any Fiero shows in this area that weekend?<BR>Thanks Oreif,<BR>Mike||||reg||4
Z||000003||Oreif||01-30-2001||11:58 PM||||I think the "Orphan Show" is the 19th and the GTO "all-Pontiac" Show is the 26th. These are unconfirmed dates.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SloPonti||01-31-2001||12:22 AM||||hey mike i was there last year and besides the rain it was a great event! i think the purpose of your show was to get together and maybe get some public attention to our cars! an idea for thought would be to move the show to peoria illinois-it is 20 mins from your town! as you know peoria is bigger and i know target has car shows from time to time there and i know they would let us have a fiero show there! this would be better in the respect that our cars would get more public attention! the location of the show last year did not really bring the public to the show-but it was great for other fiero ownders to meet each other! also another great spot would be the neil norton pontiac dealership-i have a friend that works there and i should be able to get permission to get a show there! one more spot would be sams club parking lot in willow knolls! i can help set anything up so if you need help give me a call on my cell phone at 309-264-2311 or email me! thanks mike<BR>Rob<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||MikeSchaefer||01-31-2001||12:59 AM||||I think I'm going to be keeping it in El Paso, the city is really good to me about this and it is a great center location.<BR>Hope to see you there, I love your car<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
